From cff5e76bd5678203d60dea54ce3f1fb2cf843710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Kozemchuk Ivan (CSS ICW SW SCV BFS SFW / EE)"
 <Ivan.Kozemchuk-EE@infineon.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 12:17:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] IFX: Add MXCRYPTO transparent accelerator driver hooks

Ports the IFX_PSA_MXCRYPTO_PRESENT conditional regions from
ifx-mbedtls onto the tf-psa-crypto layout, wiring the Infineon
MXCRYPTO transparent hardware accelerator (driver ID 6) into the
PSA driver wrapper dispatch for sign/verify_message, sign/verify_hash,
cipher_*, hash_*, aead_*, mac_*, asymmetric_encrypt/decrypt,
key_agreement, generate_key and public key export.

All additions are guarded by IFX_PSA_MXCRYPTO_PRESENT (and feature
sub-flags like IFX_PSA_MXCRYPTO_CIPHER, _SHA, _AEAD, _MAC, _ECDSA_SIGN,
_ECDSA_VERIFY, _KEY_GENERATION, _RSA_ENCRYPT, _RSA_DECRYPT, _ECDH,
_PUBLIC_KEY_EXPORT) so the patch is a no-op when the macro is
undefined.
